==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|en|diphthérie}}, coined 1857 by [[w:Pierre Bretonneau|Pierre Bretonneau]]; from {{etyl|grc|-}}
{{m|grc|διφθέρα||prepared hide, leather}}, for the tough membrane that forms in the throat. Bretonneau earlier used {{m|fr|diphthérite}}, from which {{m|en|diphtheritis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪfˈθɪəɹɪə/|/dɪpˈθɪəɹɪə/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/dɪfˈθiɚɹiə/|/dɪpˈθiɚɹiə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A highly [[infectious]] disease of the upper [[respiratory tract]] characterised by a sore throat, fever, and difficulty breathing, its symptoms being due to a potent [[toxin]] excreted by the infecting agent {{taxlink|Corynebacterium diphtheriae|species|noshow=1}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|repiratory tract infection}} {{l|en|Boulogne sore throat}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}, [[diphtheritis]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|diphtherial}}
* {{l|en|diphtheric}}
* {{l|en|diphtheritic}}

